#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:40
#: 0ad347de1cf6414d9497e1d0f47d3ba1
msgid "Install firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:42
#: d9c6a79b667e47bfa5a95bfb5a51cd75
msgid "In Mission Planner's **SETUP \\| Install Firmware** screen select the appropriate icon that matches your vehicle or frame type(i.e. Quad, Hexa). Answer **Yes** when it asks you \"Are you sure?\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:49
#: da5c8487a8d7417eb03aa3472fd81040
msgid "Mission Planner: Install FirmwareScreen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:51
#: c2b369c51afa4300826e20d5947b96b7
msgid "some boards are specifically targeted to a particular vehicle type and firmware is not automatically built for other vehicles. However, ArduPilot could still be built for those other vehicles using the `Custom Firmware Server <https://custom.ardupilot.org/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:53
#: 865dc0603d874df3b7004e70c85f3b2f
msgid "Mission Planner will try to detect which board you are using. It may ask you to unplug the board, press OK, and plug it back in to detect the board type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:58
#: 82e7fad9f7fe4236a414fb666424208e
msgid "Mission Planner: Install Firmware Prompt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:60
#: 963f95a10cac495aaba9e15943c635ca
msgid "Often you will be presented with a dropdown box of firmware variants for the board, which you can select from (such as bi-directional DShot variants, if available). For boards which share the Pixhawk board id, the list will be extensive, as shown below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:65
#: 049f51bd9c1949d7b0667d4270fdad09
msgid "Select the appropriate firmware for your board. For boards marked \"Pixhawk\", Pixhawk1 firmware is usually the best choice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:67
#: 89b35ceea4584cac9ca34fc7d54200d6
msgid "some boards labeled as Pixhawk 2.4.x may have sensor substitutions which may lead to pre-arm checks or no secondary IMU. Please see the BARO_OPTIONS parameter for a workaround for a known sensor substitution on some boards of a MS5607 barometer where a MS5611 should be used. IMUs may also be substituted. Where possible, please source autopilots from ArduPilot partners."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:69
#: d43dce88d00345b98ad4c9912ba9cd6d
msgid "If all goes well, you will see a status appear on the bottom right including the words: \"erase...\", \"program...\", \"verify..\", and \"Upload Done\". The firmware has been successfully uploaded to the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:71
#: 645e19f76aca45689ae5fbde635653b1
msgid "It usually takes a few seconds for the bootloader to exit and enter the main code after programming or a power-up. Wait to press CONNECT until this occurs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:73
#: 0f44b6d23336473a87fc5c7675b75410
msgid "Updating the firmware to a newer version does not alter existing parameters unless the firmware is for a different vehicle, in which case parameters are reset to their default values for that vehicle. However, it is always a good idea to save your parameters to a file using the \"Save to File\" button on the Mission Planner's **CONFIG/Full Parameter Tree** tab before any firmware updates, just in case of any issues while updating. Do not apply all parameters after upgrading to a new version as some parameters might have a different meaning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:76
#: 952d09258bad4c4b8fcf1ac9ac2d744e
msgid "Using Beta, Developer, and Customized Versions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:79
#: 6e1b83d014f54ac1bc9647b345ef5c4b
msgid "Beta"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:81
#: 5999a20b1f0c41898756972a7eee6d3f
msgid "Prior to ``Stable`` releases, ``Beta`` versions are released. These may be used if you wish to try newer features or help the developers flight test new code. Since these are \"beta\" versions, there may still be bugs. This is possible even in Stable release firmware. However, a Beta release has been tested by the development team, and already flight tested. This release allows a wider user base to final test the firmware before releasing as ``Stable``. Experienced ArduPilot users are encouraged to test fly this firmware and provide feedback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:83
#: 722a3eb4a9a442e6840d5ff651d424ad
msgid "Mission Planner has an option on the **Install Firmware** page to upload this release, but later ``Stable`` releases may already be available. Be sure to check the normal vehicle upload option first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:86
#: 9c2cd2349a704fbf97d70b392b3d94ce
msgid "Latest Developer Version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:88
#: 43ec77c67c2a4cecbff28169ce6ba035
msgid "This reflects the current state of the development branch of the ArduPilot code. It has been reviewed by the development team, passed all automated test suites, and in most cases test flown. This code gets built daily and is available for testing by experienced users. This corresponds to an \"alpha\" release, and may have bugs, although very rarely \"crash inducing\". Very shortly after an addition that changes or introduces a feature is added, the :ref:`Upcoming Features <common-master-features>` section of the Wiki is updated with information about the addition or change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:90
#: ff63d29aef0e483d87254e45a200cc2d
msgid "This code must be manually downloaded from the `Firmware Downloads <https://firmware.ardupilot.org>`__ page as ``latest`` for your particular board, and then uploaded using Mission Planner's \"Load Custom Firmware\" option on its **Install Firmware Page**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:93
#: 6951a739e3b042c1bbf3b749bf1f0b5d
msgid "Custom Firmware Build Server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:95
#: 6ee384619ea2485986c7c808488b1a06
msgid "ArduPilot is currently experimentally testing a custom firmware build server that will allow users to generate firmware builds for their autopilots with selectable features. Since all 1MB flash sized boards now have feature restrictions to allow the code to fit, this will give a path to enable a user to select which features will or will not be included, giving some flexibility to users of 1MB autopilots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:97
#: 7aed2cced4624e5f9b7e087066834cda
msgid "The server is located `HERE <https://custom.ardupilot.org>`__ and instructions for its use are :ref:`on this page HERE <common-custom-firmware>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:99
#: 0acea51f5cd246ca84538726f2d694c1
msgid "It allows creating a custom build, which can be downloaded, and flashed to the autopilot using Mission Planner's \"Load Custom Firmware\" option on its **Install Firmware Page**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:101
#: 9116ff3c67d44e6f9e0ba56cfd9caa3d
msgid "connect the ground station PC to the autopilot using a USB cable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:102
#: e9a46017700a4911801f2b1eedddba5c
msgid "select the COM port and baud rate (normally 115200, but you can choose higher if your hardware allows) for the board. These are selected on the top right of the screen.  Do **not** press the Connect button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:103
#: 06344e3b580947ef951e24cc9e4f0cbe
msgid "go to MP firmware install screen (select \"Setup >> Install Firmware\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:104
#: 8448d6ed791b41c095d3b2d94cd741a9
msgid "click the \"Load custom firmware\" link and select the .apj file you downloaded (do not select the .hex files, which are only meant to be used with DFU/JTAG/SWD methods). If the \"Load custom firmware\" link is not visible select \"Config >> Planner\" and set the \"Layout\" drop-down to \"Advanced\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:105
#: aadb67ebe7174c96b6fc3be5ec56c2be
msgid "you may need to click on \"Force bootloader\" before the step above (assuming the board has been previously flashed with Ardupilot's bootloader)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:111
#: 05e0b803d53e432da51016e1a77b59a9
msgid "follow any instructions displayed regarding plugging/unplugging the board"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:112
#: 50186af727464d918833f7d33e0b2b9f
msgid "if all goes well some status should be displayed at the bottom of the screen.  i.e. \"erase...\", \"program...\", \"verify..\" and \"Upload Done\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:115
#: a9e35a06349b49bb9a2f27abaa596be4
msgid "Firmware Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:117
#: 6997d00faf7f4896a1e8c6e8d3253b2c
msgid "For a list of what features are **not** included in the current \"latest\" firmware for any given autopilot, see :ref:`this page<binary-features>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:118
#: 24af8f2a0fef4e56ae55cacfaba58700
msgid "All the feature options currently **not** included in the 1MB autopilots, by default, are on the list of options on the Custom Firmware Build Server. There are also many features still included in the 1MB autopilots that may not be required for your application. So it is possible to create a build that includes some of the currently excluded features while removing some of the unneeded features. The list of feature options will be continuously expanded, allowing other large features to be dropped and more restricted features added to the custom build. For example, not including QuadPlane features will save space for Planes not requiring it. Drivers and peripheral support may be individually selected, allowing only those used to be in the code thus allowing other features to be included in the custom firmware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk.rst:119
#: 69e6eab9dd294784a9c7e6f676ffd4e8
msgid "Current build is from the daily master branch, Stable and Beta branches."
msgstr ""

